From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Builder <builder@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 13:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] s7d: keep the unattended boot splash clean

The BM201 HDMI console remains active after the autoboot countdown, so the
commands that follow bitmap rendering scroll the same framebuffer and push the
splash off screen.

Install a runtime-only boot command after video output multiplexing succeeds.
It routes unattended boot output back to serial before running the existing
boot flow, then restores the HDMI mux if that flow returns to the prompt. An
interrupted countdown never executes the wrapper and therefore keeps the HDMI
console interactive.
---
diff --git a/bl33/v2023/board/amlogic/s7d_bm201/s7d_bm201.c b/bl33/v2023/board/amlogic/s7d_bm201/s7d_bm201.c
--- a/bl33/v2023/board/amlogic/s7d_bm201/s7d_bm201.c
+++ b/bl33/v2023/board/amlogic/s7d_bm201/s7d_bm201.c
@@ -292,6 +292,17 @@ int board_late_init(void)
 
 	printf("HDMI console: serial and video output enabled\n");
 
+	ret = env_set("bootcmd",
+		      "setenv stdout serial; setenv stderr serial; "
+		      "run boot_default; "
+		      "setenv stdout serial,vidconsole; "
+		      "setenv stderr serial,vidconsole");
+	if (ret) {
+		printf("HDMI console: failed to install clean splash boot command (%d)\n",
+		       ret);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	ret = run_command("usb start", 0);
 	if (ret) {
 		printf("HDMI console: USB start failed (%d); serial input retained\n",
